# {{ c.mcp_dist }}

An [MCP](https://modelcontextprotocol.io) server for the {{ c.title }}. It wraps the
[`{{ c.dist }}`](https://pypi.org/project/{{ c.dist }}/) Python SDK and exposes one tool per
API method, named `<resource>_<method>`:

{% for t in c.tools %}
- `{{ t.name }}`: {{ t.title }}
{% endfor %}

## Install

```sh
pip install {{ c.mcp_dist }}
```

Requires Python 3.10 or newer.

## Run

The server speaks MCP over stdio. It reads credentials from environment variables, for whichever
auth scheme you use:

{% for a in c.ctor_args %}
- `{{ a.env }}`: {{ a.doc }}
{% endfor %}

```sh
{% for a in c.ctor_args[:1] %}
export {{ a.env }}=...
{% endfor %}
{{ c.mcp_dist }}
```

Example client configuration:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "{{ c.pkg }}": {
      "command": "{{ c.mcp_dist }}"{% for a in c.ctor_args[:1] %},
      "env": { "{{ a.env }}": "..." }{% endfor %}

    }
  }
}
```

Tool results are JSON. List tools return one page and a `next_page` object: pass its entries as
arguments to get the next page (it is `null` on the last page). The stream tool reads up to
`max_events` events (10 by default) and closes the stream. Binary responses are written to the
directory in `{{ c.env_output_dir }}` (a temporary directory by default) and the tool returns the
file's path and size. Set `{{ c.env_base_url }}` to point the server at a different API host.
